Sophon-Realtime-32B-E2E (docs/deploy.md) downloads model weights derived from the following works, each licensed under the
Apache License 2.0:
- base/ and adapters/: derived from Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct by the Qwen team, Alibaba
  (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-32B-Instruct), via DuplexJev-32B-Para (Adventists.ai). The audio encoder is derived from
  Qwen3-ASR (Qwen team, Alibaba).
- talker220/: the talker (model.safetensors) is by Adventists.ai. Its text embedding table (embed.safetensors) and tokenizer are
  taken from DuplexJev-4B-Para (Adventists.ai), which is derived from Qwen3-4B by the Qwen team, Alibaba
  (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-4B).
- e2/: the decoder is derived from the flow model of Fun-CosyVoice3-0.5B by the FunAudioLLM team, Alibaba
  (https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice), distilled to a few steps with our own input adapter; the HiFT vocoder comes from
  the same work.

Third-party code:
- sophon_expressive/cosyvoice_lite/ and sophon_expressive/hift_abs.py include code adapted from CosyVoice
  (FunAudioLLM team, Alibaba; https://github.com/FunAudioLLM/CosyVoice; Apache License 2.0).
- live/sophon_live/silero_vad.onnx is the Silero VAD model (Silero Team; https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad; MIT License).
- The tag/ and flash/ plugins run on vLLM and vLLM-Omni (Apache License 2.0), which are installed as dependencies and not
  redistributed here.
